      ],
      "responses": [
        "AskCampus offers a few scholarship categories:\n1. Merit-Based Scholarships -- Entrance scholarships for incoming students (often a 100% tuition waiver for Valedictorians or top 1% entrance scorers, 50% for Salutatorians or high scorers), plus continuing scholarships for enrolled students who maintain a required GPA/GWA with a full course load, re-evaluated each semester or academic year.\n2. Need-Based Financial Aid -- Tuition discounts (e.g. 25%, 50%, or 100%) based on documented household income.\n3. Talent, Athletic, and Cultural Grants -- Athletic scholarships for varsity student-athletes (tiered by performance/division, from partial unit discounts to full tuition and board), and grants for active members of major university organizations like the marching band, chorale/glee club, orchestra, or theater/dance groups.\nFor more information, please refer to the guidelines on the admission page."
      ],
